---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <div class="shell simple-page">
    <article class="plain-content">
      <p>I live in Seattle and work on AI agents in <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/">Visual Studio Code</a> and <a href="https://github.com/features/copilot">GitHub Copilot</a> at Microsoft. I focus on agent products, evaluation, and OpenTelemetry-based observability.</p>

      <p>My public work includes <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/agents/guides/monitoring-agents">agent monitoring in VS Code</a>, <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/enterprise/ai-settings#_configure-telemetry-export-with-opentelemetry">enterprise telemetry export</a>, and an analysis of <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/blogs/2026/06/19/what-50000-runs-taught-us">what 50,000 repeated agent-evaluation runs taught us</a>. James Newton-King’s <a href="https://opentelemetry.io/blog/2026/genai-observability/">official OpenTelemetry GenAI walkthrough</a> uses VS Code instrumentation I worked on together with the Aspire Dashboard’s GenAI visualizer.</p>

      <p>I’m currently building <strong>OTelux</strong>, a local-first telemetry workbench for developers and coding agents; <strong>Deskpal</strong>, verified computer use for Linux desktop applications; and <strong>pi-otel</strong>, vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry instrumentation for the Pi coding agent. Their repositories will become public with their initial releases.</p>

      <p>I also build learning projects. <a href="https://b1tank.github.io/learnc/">Learn C</a> is a hand-written, runnable companion to K&amp;R, and <a href="https://b1tank.github.io/learn-ghostty/">Learn Ghostty</a> is a visual, source-backed path through terminal architecture.</p>

      <p>Other projects include <a href="/projects/opensnipping/demo/">OpenSnipping</a>, <a href="https://github.com/b1tank/openmathboard">OpenMathBoard</a>, <a href="https://lezhiweng.com">BoringBlog</a>, and <a href="/projects/abc/demo/">ABC Balloon</a>. I publish reusable <a href="https://github.com/b1tank/skills">AI-agent skills</a> for the coding tools and workflows I use.</p>

      <p>Before developer tools, I worked on cloud infrastructure, distributed tracing, and Azure Managed Grafana. My route into software began in chemical engineering and scientific computing, including a <a href="https://github.com/b1tank/coag">C++ aerosol model</a> that ran 90% faster than its legacy Fortran implementation.</p>

      <p>Outside work, I enjoy basketball, billiards, and studying how Stephen Curry makes impossible geometry look routine.</p>

      <p>You can find me on <a href="https://github.com/b1tank">GitHub</a>, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhichao-li-engineer">LinkedIn</a>, and <a href="https://x.com/w5hirt">X</a>, or email <button class="inline-email" type="button"><code>{'b1tank${StephenCurry.jerseyNumber}@gmail.com'}</code></button>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <script>
    document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.inline-email')?.addEventListener('click', async (event) => {
      const button = event.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
      const email = ['zhichli', String(6 * 5), '@gmail.com'].join('');
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(email);
      const original = button.textContent;
      button.textContent = 'copied';
      window.setTimeout(() => button.textContent = original, 1400);
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
